  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Nan has $464M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, spread across 26 awards with an average award size of $17.9M. Nan's obligations are down 12.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $464M; the General Services Administration appears as a much smaller buyer with $26.4K. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is Nan's largest market at $277M, followed by Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $183M. Nan also has activity in Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $3.6M and Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction at $159K. Fiscal-year trends show that Nan moved from $22M in FY21 to $240M in FY22, $347M in FY23, $160M in FY24, $529M in FY25, and $464M in FY26. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. The figures on this page represent contract obligations except where award-value totals are explicitly called out as total contract values in the tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying from Nan?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $464M. The General Services Administration is a secondary buyer, obligating $26.4K. No other agencies are listed in the top buying agencies table for FY2026 to date. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and work areas does Nan supply to the government?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest market for Nan at $277M. Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction is the second market at $183M. Nan also has obligations in Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $3.6M and Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction at $159K."
      }
    ]
  },
